# gnome-control-center 1:50.3-0ubuntu0.2 patch for Pi-Desktop (current build: +pd3.3)
Power panel: a "Screensaver" group replaces Automatic Screen Blank. Text: "Pi-Desktop uses a screensaver instead of
blanking the screen." (+pd3.3, 2026-09-26; +pd3.2 said the display could not resume at 4K@120 Hz — fixed by kernel
patches 0010/0011, wording changed.)

Rebuild on an Orange Pi 5B booted from SD, with a spare eMMC: copy pidesktop-power-screensaver.patch and
rebuild-settings.sh into one folder and run `sudo bash rebuild-settings.sh`. It creates an Ubuntu 26.04 build root at
/srv/pd3-build on the eMMC if missing (debootstrap, build-deps, apt source; first run ~9 min incl. build), applies the
patch as the last quilt patch, bumps the version (edit VER in the script for the next one) and leaves the three .debs
next to the script. Nothing is installed on the running system; the eMMC's own OS is untouched apart from /srv/pd3-build.
Debs -> overlay/pidesktop/debs/gcc/ (only one version there: the recipe installs by glob). Re-do whenever Ubuntu ships
a new gnome-control-center (apt-mark hold keeps ours meanwhile).
